  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>Serverless means the servers are somebody else's problem, not that they are absent. You gain scale to zero, automatic concurrency and no patching. You accept cold starts, statelessness, execution limits and a bill that follows usage rather than time. It fits bursty and intermittent work, and it stops fitting when the traffic becomes steady enough that a rented machine would have been busy anyway.</p>
